# ALL.mask -- R-409 line masks for this container (entry<TAB>L<n>-or-python-regex<TAB>reason); the same rules on the oracle's stream and on SCRIP's, a masked line replaced by its marker and never deleted.
variable-size-get	PART:^type=\S+ \*x=\S+ bytes allocated=(-?[0-9]+)$	the byte count iconx reports for a value is its own allocator's block size, a machine value no program computes and SCRIP does not impersonate: MEASURED 2026-11-17 on SCRIP cdd18cb229, variable-size-get run on the oracle iconx and on SCRIP gives eight lines of type=T *x=N bytes allocated=B, every T and N equal and only B different (string 32 against the oracle's 8, the empty cset 0 against 48, the lists 160, 208 and 224 against 224, 128 and 144, the set 320 against 336), both ending in run-time error 108 at line 17 with status 1; masked in both streams, only the number, so the type, the size and the words stay graded (Lon 2026-11-17 13:4x CST: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes.")
knapsack-problem-0-1	PART:^Performance: time=(\d+) ms collections=\d+$	iconx prints how long the run took, a clock reading that no program computes: MEASURED 2026-11-17 on the oracle, run twice, time=5090 and time=4930 with every other line equal; masked in both streams, only the number
knapsack-problem-0-1	PART:^Performance: time=\d+ ms collections=(\d+)$	the count of garbage collections is the runtime's own, a machine value SCRIP's collector does not impersonate (MEASURED 2026-11-17 the oracle prints 799 in both runs); masked in both streams, only the number
linux-cpu-utilization	PART:^Overall utilization:\s+([0-9.]+)%$	the share of the machine's cpu time since boot, read from /proc/stat: a value of the machine that moves between two runs (MEASURED 2026-11-17 on the oracle, 78.72058636 and another figure in the next run); masked, only the number
linux-cpu-utilization	PART:^Interval utilization:\s+([0-9.]+)%$	the share of cpu time over the program's own interval read from /proc/stat, a machine value that moves between runs (MEASURED 2026-11-17: 99.375 in one run, another in the next); masked, only the number
